tlas Cherif","grocery",31.62889,-7.98684,"190 Rahba Kedima Square, 40000","","","","","s"],["Daba Daba","restaurant",31.62623,-7.98696,"","","","","","f"],["Herboristerie Arganie","cosmetics",31.62633,-7.98691,"","","","","","s"],["Terrasse Bakchich","restaurant",31.63094,-7.98696,"294 Souq Talaa","Mo-Su 10:00-22:00","+212 6 67 05 54 05","","","f"],["Chez Leon","ice cream",31.62997,-7.98895,"","","","","","f"],["Rahba Kedima Square","attraction",31.62888,-7.98705,"","","","","","a"],["Café des épices","cafe",31.62905,-7.98732,"75 Derb Rahba Lakdima","Mo-Su 09:00-23:00","06 62 56 41 34","","international;moroccan","f"],["Almoravid Qubba (Almoravid Koubba القبة المرابطية)","ruins",31.63146,-7.98716,"","","","","","a"],["Terrasse La Medersa","restaurant",31.63209,-7.98597,"","","","","","f"],["Tavlin","restaurant",31.6307,-7.98631,"","","","","","f"],["Medersa Ben Youssef","attraction",31.63198,-7.98625,"","09:00-18:00; PH closed \"religous holidays\"","","","","a"],["Marrakech Museum (Musée de Marrakech متحف مراكش)","museum",31.63155,-7.98607,"","09:00-18:30","+212 244418","","","a"],["Medina","sight",31.63318,-7.98869,"","","","","","r","The Medina is the old city quarter located within the sandstone city walls that give Marrakech the nickname the Red City. As an ancient hub, it contains a maze of narrow streets and outdoor marketplaces."],["Djemaa El-Fna","sight",31.62604,-7.98903,"","","","","","r","The highlight of any Marrakech night. Musicians, dancers, and story tellers pack this square at the heart of the medina, filling it with a cacophony of drum beats and excited shouts. Scores of stalls sell a wide array of Moroccan fare…"],["The Souks","sight",31.6271,-7.98727,"","","","","","r","Markets of Marrakech, just adjacent to Place Djemaa El-Fna, are where you can buy almost anything, from spices to shoes, jellabas to kaftans, and tea pots to tagines. Undoubtedly, being a foreigner means you will end up paying higher…"],["Koutoubia Mosque","sight",31.6237,-7.9935,"","","","","","r","Named after the booksellers market that used to be located here. It is said that the minaret of the Koutoubia mosque is to Marrakech as the Eiffel Tower is to Paris. The minaret is visible from Gueliz which is connected to the Medina by…"],["Moroccan Culinary Arts Museum","sight",31.62158,-7.98425,"Rue Riad Zitoun el Jdid","","","","","r","If you are interested in food and eating culture, you will enjoy this museum. Audiovisual information about the rich culinary culture of Marocco, its ingredients, techniques and traditions. You can also touch and smell many things. They…"],["Dar Si Saïd Museum","sight",31.62341,-7.98386,"","10:00–18:00","","","","r","Museum set in an old palace with beautiful gardens. While somewhat run-down, it is worth seeing and houses many different artifacts from Morocco through the ages, such as wood carvings, musical instruments, and weapons. It is dedicated…"],["Ben Youssef Madrasa","sight",31.63203,-7.98618,"Kaat Benahid","09:00–19:00 daily (during Ramadan 09:00–16:30), closed for religious holidays","","","","r","One of the largest madrassas in North Africa. It is a school attached to the Ben Youssef Mosque and is home to beautiful art and architecture. The present building was completed in 1564–1565 under the Saadian sultan Abdallah al-Ghalib,…"],["El Bahia Palace","sight",31.62089,-7.98414,"","09:00–17:00","","","","r","An ornate palace complex built in the late 19th century, with courtyards, gardens, richly decorated rooms and traditional Moroccan architectural details. The palace was begun in the 1860s by Si Moussa, grand vizier to Sultan Muhammad…"],["Jewish Cemetery","sight",31.62006,-7.98018,"Avenue Taoulat El Miara","09:00-17:00","","","","r","The largest Jewish cemetery in Morocco, characterized by white-washed tombs and sandy graves. The men selling tickets are full of interesting information about the cemetery but you have to ask."],["Slat Al Azama Synagogue","sight",31.62017,-7.98238,"","09:00-19:00 (closed Sat)","","","","r","Synagogue which is not only a place of worship with a beautiful open courtyard, but also includes interesting displays about Judaism's varied history in Morocco, including photos of Jews in the Berber Mountains."],["Marrakech Museum","sight",31.63158,-7.98633,"","09:00-18:30","","","","r","It's housed in the Dar Menebhi Palace, constructed at the end of the 19th century."],["Ali Ben Youssef Mosque","sight",31.63192,-7.98716,"","","","","","r","The first mosque in Marrakesh was erected at this place by the Almoravid emir Yusuf ibn Tashfin in the 1070s. However, it was almost completely rebuilt in early 19th century by the Alaouite sultan Suleiman, with hardly any trace left of…"],["Almoravid Koubba","sight",31.6315,-7.9872,"","","","","","r","A very small but intricate domed pavilion, known for being the only surviving example of Almoravid religious architecture (early 12th century) in Marrakech. Located across the street from the Ben Youssef Mosque, it is believed to have…"],["Chez Bismilah","restaurant",31.63085,-7.987,"193 Souk El kebir","","","","","r","Amazing food and wonderful service. The owner is very kind and the fantastic chef is a humble lady who cooks perfectly all the traditional Moroccan recipes. Tayine Royale is recommended. The roof top has an amazing view over the old medina."],["Café Babouche medina","restaurant",31.62631,-7.98696,"37 Rue des Banques","","","","","r","In a small street a few steps from the Jemaa El Fna square. You can eat there in a friendly atmosphere. The veal tagine with prunes and almonds is spectacular."],["sky mabrouka","restaurant",31.62367,-7.98949,"","","","","","r","Serves the same standard fare as everywhere else in a little courtyard or terrace."],["Le Marrakchi","restaurant",31.62655,-7.98712,"Place jeema el-fna, 52 Rue des Banques","","","","","r","With two main courses and wine running at around 300 dirham, this is one of the poshest restaurants in the square. The food is not necessarily better than elsewhere, but it is one of the few restaurants that serves alcohol. It also has…"],["Dar Najat's Kitchen","restaurant",31.62389,-7.98346,"Douar Groua, derb lalla chacha, N.18","","","","","r","Daily fresh food in a boutique riad."],["Hotel Grand Tazi","bar",31.6225,-7.98953,"Rue Bab Agnaou","","","","","r","The hotel has a public bar, serving beer and wine and is not overly expensive."]]}